Sval: WebDriver opens a window in any build with Firefox's application ID

WindowManager.openBrowserWindow, which WebDriver classic's NewWindow and
BiDi's browsingContext.create({type: "window"}) both reach, switched on
AppInfo.name and handled only "Firefox". Sval's name is "Sval", so every
WebDriver client failed with "openWindow() not supported in Sval". The rest
of the remote agent, opening and closing tabs among it, tests
AppInfo.isFirefox, which compares the application ID that Sval keeps, and so
does this. mozilla-central's openBrowserWindow is unchanged; drop the patch
once Mozilla fixes it. No chrome API reaches inside the remote agent, so a
patch is the only fix.

